'' A BARE 'width' IN VALUE POSITION IS A CALL, exactly as 'width( )' is. It has no
'' declaration, so LowerBareProcCall_ -- which asks the symbol -- never saw it, and the
'' statement around it was dropped: starshine.bas's 'var wd = loword( width )' left wd
'' uninitialised. See the source.
''
'' MEASURED, fbc-modern 1.20 -gen gcc -r:
''
''     int32 vr$0 = fb_Width( -1, -1 );  A$0 = vr$0;
''     int32 vr$2 = fb_Width( -1, -1 );  F$0 = (uint64)vr$2 & 65535ull;
''
'' Every use below lowers to that call; none is dropped.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/mir/src/bare-width-value.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: verify: ok
'' EXPECT-OUT: 0 statements not lowered
'' EXPECT-OUT: call.rtl i32 fb_Width(-1, -1)
